    "description": "Try-catch is a PHP command, which runs a block of code, and catches some configured exceptions that the block may throw. It may be completed with a finally block.\n\nThe catch clause may be anonymous, when it only specifies the type of caught exception, without providing a variable name.\n",
    "code": "<?php\n\ntry {\n    callSomeMethod();\n} catch (\\Exception $e) {\n    // process the error here\n}\n\n?>",
